      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Tilda Newra</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle reaches its destination, the delivery handover must capture the vehicle’s exact condition, mileage and formal acceptance.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The process is divided into three core checks – daylight condition re‑inspection, odometer verification, and a signed condition sign‑off – each of which is documented against the original pickup photographs and the LR (Logistics Receipt) bilty.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
<li><strong>Daylight condition re‑inspection against pickup photos</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Arrange the handover in a well‑lit area under natural daylight to eliminate shadows that could hide surface damage.</li>
        <li>Open the vehicle’s storage compartment and compare every panel, tyre, chain, and accessory with the high‑resolution pickup images taken at origin.</li>
        <li>Note any new scratches, dents, paint chips, or broken parts on an inspection sheet. Use a magnifying glass for small blemishes on the fuel tank, head‑light lenses and chrome trims.</li>
        <li>Photograph the vehicle from the angles as the pickup set; label each new photo with the date, time and handover location for audit trails.</li>
    </ul></div>
